# E-commerce Retention Analysis

## Overview

This project analyzes a synthetic e-commerce dataset to assess customer retention, repeat purchases, and cohort performance.

## File structure

```text
data/
├── generate_sample_data.py
├── customers.csv
├── orders.csv
├── order_items.csv
├── products.csv
```

## Data generation script

The data is generated using a reproducible Python script. It creates realistic customer acquisition patterns over multiple months and a mixture of repeat and one-time buyers.

Run:

```bash
python data/generate_sample_data.py
```

## Notes

- Customers are assigned acquisition channels: Organic, Paid, Referral, Social.
- Product categories include Electronics, Fashion, Home, Beauty, Sports.
- Orders are distributed over several months and include a mix of return and repeat behaviors.
- The dataset is intentionally synthetic and suitable for SQL and Python analysis.
